{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"Any change touching a `global_support` path selects EVERY mutation shard, and the resulting\nrun exceeds the mutation job's `timeout-minutes: 30`. GitHub reports the timed-out job as\n`cancelled`, and the CI bot turns that into a `Verified -1` that carries no test signal. The\nfailure is DETERMINISTIC, so `recheck` can never clear it.\n\n## Proof\n\n`.github/mutation-shards.toml` declares `global_support`, which includes\n`.github/workflows/test.yml`, `pyproject.toml`, `uv.lock`, `tests/conftest.py`,\n`tests/**/conftest.py`, `scripts/mutation_gate.py`, and three workflow files.\n\n`scripts/mutation_gate.py::select_shards` starts:\n\n    if any(_matches(path, pattern) for path in changed_paths for pattern in manifest.global_support):\n        names = tuple(manifest.shards)\n\nSo ONE touched global-support path selects all 7 shards, overriding the `all-shards: false`\nworkflow input that exists precisely to keep the gate bounded.\n\nMeasured on Gerrit change 1615 (which edits `.github/workflows/test.yml` among others):\n\n    total shards: 7 -> signing, reducer-processors, next-batch, gates, validate,\n                       compact-policy, push-policy\n    SELECTED: all 7  => all shards selected? True\n\nTwo independent runs of that change died at exactly the timeout, which is what distinguishes a\ntimeout from a race:\n\n| Run | mutation job | duration | outcome |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 31560638673 | 03:39:25 -> 04:09:41 | 30m16s | cancelled |\n| 31562494026 | 04:16:23 -> 04:46:40 | 30m17s | cancelled |\n\nEach shard runs a base AND a head mutation pass, so selecting all 7 means 14 passes in a\n30-minute budget.\n\n## Correction to the first filing\n\nThis ticket originally attributed the cancellation to a Verified Gate concurrency group not\nkeyed per-change, because the first cancellation coincided to the second with another run's\ncreation. That was a coincidence and is REFUTED: the second occurrence cancelled at the same\n30-minute mark with no run created at that moment, and `_mutation.yml:34` declares\n`timeout-minutes: 30`. There is no evidence of cross-change cancellation.\n\n## Impact\n\n`pyproject.toml` and `uv.lock` are in `global_support`, so every dependency bump hits this, as\ndoes any change to `tests/conftest.py` or the listed workflows. Those changes cannot obtain a\n`Verified +1` at all, and each attempt burns a full 30-minute runner slot. Gerrit change 1615\nis blocked on exactly this.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] AC1: a change touching a single `global_support` path completes the mutation gate within\n      its job timeout, or is explicitly and visibly skipped rather than failing.\n- [ ] AC2: the fix is chosen deliberately among: raising `timeout-minutes` to fit a measured\n      all-shards run; pruning `global_support` to paths that genuinely change mutation\n      semantics (a CI lane definition like `test.yml` arguably does not); sharding the\n      all-shards case across parallel jobs; or bounding the all-shards selection.\n- [ ] AC3: a timed-out or cancelled mutation job does not produce `Verified -1` as though it\n      were a test verdict, or the vote message states plainly that the gate did not complete.\n- [ ] AC4: reproduce first - a change touching only `.github/workflows/test.yml` must be shown\n      selecting all 7 shards and exceeding 30 minutes - then show the fix resolves it.\n- [ ] AC5: verify the fix does not require the fixing change itself to pass the broken gate\n      (`_mutation.yml`, `mutation-shards.toml`, and `mutation_gate.py` are all themselves in\n      `global_support`, so the repair is self-blocking and may need an admin path).","title":"Mutation gate times out: one global_support path selects ALL shards, exceeding timeout-minutes 30"}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1786510274739098001,"uuid":"b8e48cd7-5307-4068-8b25-48ac57dab2f4"}